  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Mukesh Rathore vs Union Of India on 8 April, 2024 Author: Subodh Abhyankar Bench: Subodh Abhyankar 1 In The High Court Of Madhya Pradesh At Indore BEFORE HON'BLE SHRI JUSTICE SUBODH ABHYANKAR ON THE 8 th OF APRIL, 2024 WRIT PETITION No. 7680 of 2024 BETWEEN:- MUKESH RATHORE S/O ASHOK RATHORE OCCUPATION: BUSINESS SENDHWA, TEHSIL SENDHWA DISTRICT BARWANI (MADHYA PRADESH) .. (BY SHRI AKSHAT SHARMA - ADVOCATE) AND 1. UNION OF INDIA SECRETARY MINISTRY OF COMMERCE AND INDUSTRY PETROLEUM AND EXPLOSIVE SAFETY ORGANISATION (PESO) E-7/77, II FLOOR, LALA LAJPAT RAI SOCIETY, NEAR 12 NUMBER BUS STOP, ARERA COLONY, BHOPAL (MADHYA PRADESH) 2. STATE OF MADHYA PRADESH THROUGH PRINCIPAL SECRETARY DEPARTMENT OF FOOD CIVIL SUPPLIERS AND CONSUMER PROTECTION VALLABH BHAWAN BHOPAL (MADHYA PRADESH) 3. COLLECTOR BARWANI (MADHYA PRADESH) 4 . SUB DIVISIONAL OFFICER REVENUE SENDHWA DIST BARWANI (MADHYA PRADESH) ..... (BY MS. SURBHI BAHEL - ADVOCATE FOR RESPONDENT NO.1/UOI AND MS. PRANJALI YAJURVEDI - P.L. FOR STATE) This petition coming on for admission this day, th e co following: ORDER 1. Heard. Mukesh Rathore vs Union Of India on 8 April, 2024 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/71472444/ 1 2. This writ petition under Article 226 of the Constitution of India has been filed by the petitioner seeking the following reliefs:- \"a) To allow this petition by issuing appropriate writ, direction or order, and to direct the Collector, Khargone to conclude the proceedings of Case No. 0083/B- 121/2023-24, without any further delay and decide the matter in accordance with law; and b) Anyother relief which this Court may deem fit in favour of the petitioner in the interest of justice.\" 3.",
    "facts": "The grievance of the petitioner is that the petitioner's godown has been seized by the Collector before whom Case No.083/B-121/2023-24 is still pending, which is causing extremely hardship to the petitioner.",
    "arguments": ""
  },
